[1m[38;5;231mWhat makes a task one the user "cares about"?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mImplicit + explicit follow (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mCreating or being assigned a task auto-subscribes you; a follow/unfollow toggle covers everything else. Subscriber
[39m     [38;5;246mset stored per task.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Explicit subscribe only
     [38;5;246mNothing notifies until the user stars/follows a task. Simplest model, zero noise, but silent until the user acts.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Implicit by ownership only
     [38;5;246mYou hear about tasks you created or were assigned. No follow UI at all. Smallest surface; can't track others' [39m
     [38;5;246mtasks.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Rule-based filters
     [38;5;246mSubscribe to tags, priorities, or queries rather than individual tasks. Most powerful, substantially more [39m
